{"id":"08e8a43c15b7f036","group":"58","path":"58/batch03/58-df-zfc-model9-elementary-submodel-fragment.md","title":"ZFC Model9 Elementary Submodel Fragment","display":"df-zfc-model9-elementary-submodel-fragment — ZFC Model9 Elementary Submodel Fragment","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-model9-elementary-submodel-fragment","aliases":["58-df-zfc-model9-elementary-submodel-fragment"],"display":"df-zfc-model9-elementary-submodel-fragment — ZFC Model9 Elementary Submodel Fragment","depends_on":["[[58-df-assignment]]","[[58-df-formula]]","[[58-df-satisfaction]]","[[58-df-substructure]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-model9-elementary-submodel-fragment"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-model9-elementary-submodel-fragment</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-model9-elementary-submodel-fragment — ZFC Model9 Elementary Submodel Fragment"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"64f35ba2e87964e0\" href=\"?note=64f35ba2e87964e0\" title=\"58-df-assignment\">58-df-assignment</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"58-df-formula\">58-df-formula</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"8b6a90316aad78a4\" href=\"?note=8b6a90316aad78a4\" title=\"58-df-satisfaction\">58-df-satisfaction</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"563f382027630287\" href=\"?note=563f382027630287\" title=\"58-df-substructure\">58-df-substructure</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M,N,\\Phi,L,\\operatorname{Val}_M,\\operatorname{Sat}_M,\\operatorname{Val}_N,\\operatorname{Sat}_N\\in V\">\\(M,N,\\Phi,L,\\operatorname{Val}_M,\\operatorname{Sat}_M,\\operatorname{Val}_N,\\operatorname{Sat}_N\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S\\subseteq V^4\">\\(\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S\\subseteq V^4\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"8b6a90316aad78a4\" href=\"?note=8b6a90316aad78a4\" title=\"58-df-satisfaction\">58-df-satisfaction</a>), <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Assign}\">\\(\\mathrm{Assign}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"64f35ba2e87964e0\" href=\"?note=64f35ba2e87964e0\" title=\"58-df-assignment\">58-df-assignment</a>), <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Substructure}_S\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{Substructure}_S\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"563f382027630287\" href=\"?note=563f382027630287\" title=\"58-df-substructure\">58-df-substructure</a>), and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Fml}_S(L)\">\\(\\mathrm{Fml}_S(L)\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"58-df-formula\">58-df-formula</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcModel9ElementarySubmodelFragment}_S:V^3\\to\\mathsf{Bool}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcModel9ElementarySubmodelFragment}_S:V^3\\to\\mathsf{Bool}\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}model9\\text{-}elementary\\text{-}submodel\\text{-}fragment}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcModel9ElementarySubmodelFragment}_S(M,N,\\Phi)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists L,\\operatorname{Val}_M,\\operatorname{Sat}_M,\n\\operatorname{Val}_N,\\operatorname{Sat}_N\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Substructure}_S(M,N,L)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S(M,L,\\operatorname{Val}_M,\\operatorname{Sat}_M)\n\\land\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S(N,L,\\operatorname{Val}_N,\\operatorname{Sat}_N)\n\\land\\Phi\\subseteq\\mathrm{Fml}_S(L)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall s\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Assign}(M,s)\\to\n\\mathrm{Assign}(N,s)\n\\land\\forall\\varphi\\in\\Phi\\;\n\\bigl(\\operatorname{Sat}_M(\\varphi,s)\n\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{Sat}_N(\\varphi,s)\\bigr)\n\\Bigr)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}model9\\text{-}elementary\\text{-}submodel\\text{-}fragment}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcModel9ElementarySubmodelFragment}_S(M,N,\\Phi)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists L,\\operatorname{Val}_M,\\operatorname{Sat}_M,\n\\operatorname{Val}_N,\\operatorname{Sat}_N\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Substructure}_S(M,N,L)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S(M,L,\\operatorname{Val}_M,\\operatorname{Sat}_M)\n\\land\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S(N,L,\\operatorname{Val}_N,\\operatorname{Sat}_N)\n\\land\\Phi\\subseteq\\mathrm{Fml}_S(L)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall s\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Assign}(M,s)\\to\n\\mathrm{Assign}(N,s)\n\\land\\forall\\varphi\\in\\Phi\\;\n\\bigl(\\operatorname{Sat}_M(\\varphi,s)\n\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{Sat}_N(\\varphi,s)\\bigr)\n\\Bigr)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Both structures share one explicit language and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span> is required to be an actual substructure of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"N\">\\(N\\)</span>, not merely to have a smaller carrier.  Their satisfaction recursions remain separately typed and are compared only on assignments from <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion"